[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Security operations
UID: APP-SOC
VERSION: 1.0.0
DATE: 2026-09-30
CLASSIFICATION: Internal
PREFIX: SOC-
ROOT: False

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: ../../grammar/org.sgra

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: How Northline assesses controls, takes vulnerabilities, grants exceptions, and keeps evidence. The control text stays in the catalog. A requirement here conforms to that catalog identifier. It does not copy the control.

[[SECTION]]
UID: SOC-SEC-ASM
PREFIX: ASM
TITLE: Assessments

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SOC-ASM-001
TITLE: Claim set
STATEMENT: Security shall assess the controls Northline claims and shall not invent a second identifier for a catalog control.
STATUS: Active
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: ENT-SOC-001
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: PLT-OPS-001
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: CA-2
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: PL-2

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SOC-ASM-002
TITLE: Independent assessor
STATEMENT: Security shall use an assessor who did not implement the control under test.
STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: ENT-SOC-001
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: PLT-OPS-001
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: CA-2.2
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: AC-5
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: V-222578

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SOC-ASM-003
TITLE: Result
STATEMENT: Security shall record met, not met, or not applicable, and the evidence the result used.
STATUS: Active
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: ENT-SOC-001
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: PLT-OPS-004
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: CA-2
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: AU-3

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SOC-ASM-004
TITLE: Finding
STATEMENT: Security shall open a finding when a result is not met, with a due date and an owner.
STATUS: Active
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: ENT-SOC-001
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: PLT-OPS-007
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: CA-5

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SOC-ASM-005
TITLE: Inherited
STATEMENT: Security shall name the platform requirement a product inherits instead of reassessing the platform control in every app.
STATUS: Active
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: ENT-SOC-001
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: PLT-OPS-005
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: CA-2
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: PL-8

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SOC-ASM-006
TITLE: Continuous
STATEMENT: Security shall record a monitoring result between full assessments for the controls marked continuous.
STATUS: Active
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: ENT-SOC-001
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: PLT-OPS-001
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: CA-7
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: CA-7.1

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SOC-ASM-007
TITLE: Boundary
STATEMENT: Security shall list every system in the authorization boundary and shall refuse an undeclared production system.
STATUS: Active
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: ENT-SOC-007
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: PLT-OPS-005
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: PL-8
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: CM-8
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: V-222585

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SOC-ASM-008
TITLE: Plan
STATEMENT: Security shall keep one system security plan that points at this catalog and at the requirements that implement it.
STATUS: Active
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: ENT-SOC-001
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: PL-2
[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: SOC-SEC-VUL
PREFIX: VUL
TITLE: Vulnerabilities and exceptions

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SOC-VUL-001
TITLE: One queue
STATEMENT: Security shall accept scan findings into one queue and shall keep the scanner's identifier.
STATUS: Active
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: ENT-SOC-002
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: PLT-MON-001
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: RA-5

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SOC-VUL-002
TITLE: Critical clock
STATEMENT: Security shall set the enterprise patch window as the due date of a critical finding.
STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: ENT-SOC-002
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: PLT-MON-002
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: SI-2
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: RA-5
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: V-222588

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SOC-VUL-003
TITLE: False positive
STATEMENT: Security shall record why a finding was marked a false positive and who decided.
STATUS: Active
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: ENT-SOC-002
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: PLT-AUD-002
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: RA-5.2
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: AU-3

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SOC-VUL-004
TITLE: Internet first
STATEMENT: Security shall rank an internet-facing finding ahead of an internal finding of the same severity.
STATUS: Active
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: ENT-SOC-002
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: RA-5.3

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SOC-VUL-005
TITLE: Image scan
STATEMENT: Security shall block a workload image with an open critical finding from the production registry.
STATUS: Active
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: ENT-SOC-002
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: PLT-MON-005
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: RA-5
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: SI-7

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SOC-VUL-006
TITLE: Exception
STATEMENT: Security shall allow an unmet control only through an exception with an owner, a reason, and an expiry.
STATUS: Active
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: ENT-SOC-003
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: PLT-OPS-002
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: CA-5
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: RA-5

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SOC-VUL-007
TITLE: No silent renewal
STATEMENT: Security shall close an exception on its expiry and shall require a new approval to extend it.
STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: ENT-SOC-003
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: PLT-OPS-002
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: CA-5
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: V-222589

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SOC-VUL-008
TITLE: Accept a flaw
STATEMENT: Security shall review an accepted vulnerability before its expiry and shall record the residual risk.
STATUS: Active
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: ENT-SOC-008
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: PLT-OPS-002
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: RA-5
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: CA-5

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SOC-VUL-009
TITLE: Exception scope
STATEMENT: Security shall name the systems an exception covers and shall not apply it enterprise-wide by default.
STATUS: Draft
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: ENT-SOC-003
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: PLT-OPS-005
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: CA-5
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: PL-8
[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: SOC-SEC-INC
PREFIX: INC
TITLE: Incidents

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SOC-INC-001
TITLE: Open a case
STATEMENT: Security shall open a case with a severity and an owner when an incident is confirmed.
STATUS: Active
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: ENT-SOC-004
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: Refines
  VALUE: PLT-OPS-003
- TYPE: Parent
  ROLE: ConformsTo
  VALUE: IR-4
